<http://data.silknow.org/event/b885b8d7-5f95-3711-901b-2cc929b87562>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "This silk programme was produced for the matinee performance of <i>Pygmalion and Galatea</i> at the Royal Lyceum Theatre on Tuesday 12th February 1884. The three act comedy by W. S. Gilbert starred Mr J. H. Barnes as Pygmalion and Miss Mary Anderson as Galatea. This was followed by a one act drama written for Mary Anderson by W. S. Gilbert titled <i>Comedy and Tragedy</i>. The performances featured new scenery by Hawes Craven &amp; W. G. Cuthbert, costumes by Auguste et Cie. from designs by Lewis Wingfield, and original music by Musical Director Mr. Andrew Levey. The stage manager was Mr. Oliver Doud and the acting manager was Mr. Charles J. Abud."@en ;
        ecrm:P14_carried_out_by        <http://data.silknow.org/actor/4f653155-fcbf-31d4-a321-a3808ce49645> ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P23_transferred_title_from
                "Given by Dame Bridget D'Oyly Carte" ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/51c793b5-6146-3bdb-88aa-2394663fe4b9> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "This silk programme was produced for the matinee performance of <i>Pygmalion and Galatea</i> at the Royal Lyceum Theatre on Tuesday 12th February 1884. The three act comedy by W. S. Gilbert starred Mr J. H. Barnes as Pygmalion and Miss Mary Anderson as Galatea. This was followed by a one act drama written for Mary Anderson by W. S. Gilbert titled <i>Comedy and Tragedy</i>. The performances featured new scenery by Hawes Craven &amp; W. G. Cuthbert, costumes by Auguste et Cie. from designs by Lewis Wingfield, and original music by Musical Director Mr. Andrew Levey. The stage manager was Mr. Oliver Doud and the acting manager was Mr. Charles J. Abud."@en .

